# 1️⃣ What is MAC?

**MAC = Media Access Control**

It is a sublayer of the **Data Link Layer**.

Its main job:

> Decide **which device gets access to a shared communication medium**.

Imagine 20 computers connected to the same shared channel.

If everyone transmits simultaneously:

```text id="3d0k5a"
A ──┐
B ──┤
C ──┼── Shared Channel
D ──┤
E ──┘

      ↓

   COLLISION 💥
```

MAC protocols try to control this.

---

# 2️⃣ Two Types of Multiple Access

## Random Access

Devices compete for the channel.

Examples:

* ALOHA
* CSMA
* CSMA/CD
* CSMA/CA

## Controlled Access

Access is coordinated.

Examples:

* Polling
* Token passing

For GATE, **random access** is especially important.

---

# 3️⃣ ALOHA

ALOHA is one of the simplest random-access protocols.

The basic rule:

> **Transmit whenever you have data.**

No channel sensing is performed.

```text id="e2m9y6"
Data available?
      ↓
Transmit immediately
      ↓
Collision?
  /       \
No        Yes
↓          ↓
Success   Retransmit
```

---

# 4️⃣ Pure ALOHA

In Pure ALOHA:

> A station can transmit at **any time**.

This makes it simple but inefficient.

---

# 5️⃣ Vulnerable Period of Pure ALOHA

Let:

[
T
]

be the frame transmission time.

A frame can collide with another frame that starts:

```text id="d5h3zq"
T before
   ↓
[ Previous Frame ]

      [Your Frame]
            ↑
         T after
```

Therefore:

[
\boxed{Vulnerable\ Period=2T}
]

---

# 6️⃣ Pure ALOHA Throughput

The maximum throughput of Pure ALOHA is:

[
\boxed{S=Ge^{-2G}}
]

where:

* (G) = offered load
* (S) = throughput

Maximum occurs at:

[
G=\frac12
]

Therefore:

[
S_{max}=\frac{1}{2e}
]

[
\boxed{S_{max}\approx18.4%}
]

🔥 **Memorize:**

> **Pure ALOHA maximum efficiency ≈ 18.4%**

---

# 7️⃣ Slotted ALOHA

Slotted ALOHA improves Pure ALOHA.

Time is divided into slots.

```text id="7hr9z7"
| Slot 1 | Slot 2 | Slot 3 | Slot 4 |
```

A station can transmit **only at the beginning of a slot**.

---

# 8️⃣ Vulnerable Period of Slotted ALOHA

For Slotted ALOHA:

[
\boxed{Vulnerable\ Period=T}
]

instead of:

[
2T
]

Therefore efficiency improves.

---

# 9️⃣ Slotted ALOHA Throughput

Formula:

[
\boxed{S=Ge^{-G}}
]

Maximum occurs at:

[
G=1
]

Therefore:

[
S_{max}=\frac1e
]

[
\boxed{S_{max}\approx36.8%}
]

---

# 🔥 10️⃣ Pure vs Slotted ALOHA

| Feature            |   Pure ALOHA | Slotted ALOHA |
| ------------------ | -----------: | ------------: |
| Transmission       |      Anytime | Slot boundary |
| Vulnerable period  |         (2T) |           (T) |
| Maximum efficiency |        18.4% |         36.8% |
| Synchronization    | Not required |      Required |

### Golden memory:

[
\boxed{18.4% \rightarrow Pure}
]

[
\boxed{36.8% \rightarrow Slotted}
]

