# 1️⃣1️⃣ CSMA

CSMA = **Carrier Sense Multiple Access**

Unlike ALOHA:

> **Listen before transmitting.**

```text id="xwvz2n"
Want to transmit?
       ↓
Sense channel
       ↓
Busy? ───── Yes → Wait
  |
 No
  ↓
Transmit
```

This reduces collisions.

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Why Can CSMA Still Have Collisions?

Suppose two computers are far apart.

```text id="0zpykn"
A ---------------------- B
```

A checks channel → idle.

B checks channel → idle.

Both transmit almost simultaneously.

```text id="yn8w5v"
A →→→→ 💥 ←←←← B
```

Why?

Because **propagation delay** means one device may not yet know that another device has started transmitting.

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ CSMA Persistence Methods

### 1-Persistent CSMA

If channel is idle:

> Transmit immediately.

If busy:

> Keep sensing until idle, then transmit.

---

### Nonpersistent CSMA

If channel is busy:

> Wait a random amount of time, then sense again.

This reduces collision probability.

---

### p-Persistent CSMA

Used in slotted systems.

If channel is idle:

* Transmit with probability (p)
* Defer with probability (1-p)

---

# 🧠 Quick Comparison

| Protocol      | Main Idea                   |
| ------------- | --------------------------- |
| Pure ALOHA    | Transmit anytime            |
| Slotted ALOHA | Transmit at slot boundaries |
| CSMA          | Listen before transmitting  |

